    "4e68093b-95cb-4e22-9c0b-8a1da58c78e7": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "settings": {
        "subheading": "ELECTRA",
        "title": "Why static is a hazard in clinical spaces",
        "title_size": 28,
        "title_width": 12,
        "text": "<p>Medical facilities—such as intensive care units, imaging rooms, and operating theatres—require careful design to prevent electrostatic buildup. Uncontrolled static discharge can cause mild electric shocks to patients and healthcare professionals, interfere with sensitive medical equipment, and pose risks to both people and devices.</p><p></p><p><strong>ELECTRA</strong> was engineered specifically to meet this challenge. </p><p>Using state-of-the-art chemical functionalization for conductivity, this innovative upholstery fabric safely channels static electricity away, preventing electric shocks. It combines safety with comfort and hygiene —allowing medical professionals and patients to sit or lie down with confidence.</p>",
        "button_label": "ORDER FREE SAMPLES",
        "button_link": "shopify://products/electra-collection",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "text_width": 62,
        "button_style": "primary",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/electra_chair6.png",
        "image_width": 72,
        "image_position": "left",
        "media_size": "cover",
        "color_scheme": "standard",
        "color_bg": "",
        "color_text": ""
      }
    },
